  "findings": [
    "All six cached verified implementations match historical raw runtime bytes byte-for-byte. StakedUSDat current 2005 implementation was absent from old 2b707 cache; fresh Sourcify exact-match bytecode closes that specific documentation gap without re-executing deposits.",
    "Current StakedUSDat implementation explicitly reverts standard redeem/withdraw with OperationNotAllowed, using requestRedeem separately. The selected generic Family correctly reports deposit-only; asynchronous exits are not silently added. Same-N depositFeeBps=0 and paused=false were independently read; fee-recipient code can be empty EOA.",
    "The two Strata instances are tested only in deposit directions. Both standard deposit paths update CDO accounting and use underlying strategy; current same-N CDO/strategy addresses and code hashes now explicitly bound. No claim that generic redeem covers fee/cooldown/exit-mode semantics.",
    "Both Morpho VaultV2 implementations support receiver-bearing deposit/redeem; gate checks and liquidity adapter call stay protocol-owned. Both actual liquidityAdapter addresses and code hashes are pinned. maxRedeem() deliberately returns zero as conservative bound in verified source, yet successful active same-state redemption is proven; no blanket maxRedeem=0 impossibility claim.",
    "Euler beacon implementation exposes receiver-bearing ERC4626 methods routed through EVC/MODULE_VAULT. Current MODULE_VAULT/MODULE_TOKEN/EVC code bindings added. Internal EVC routing is not a Family deferred-input settlement capability; no lending/borrowing/liquidation execution added.",
    "All 144 selected successes had total share supply delta equal observed user mint/burn; all underlying supply deltas equal zero. This follows actual logs and is limited to tested states, not an assumption that fees/accrual never mint additional shares.",
    "Standard deposit uses existing MAX standing approval. Actual Approval events all grant MAX; these tests neither clear approval nor claim approval-clearance. Redeem uses caller-owned shares without an input-token approval event. No new approval policy was introduced.",
    "Full production tree23b06 (1244 entries), exact current BotVM artifact6a8295 and owner-patched runtime dbebd147 are independently rebound to each result. Node-attested source stateRoot covers invoked dependency state; targeted getter snapshots supplement, not replace actual execution."
  ],
